  "audit_notes": [
    "The first build failed because the cardinality test used WHERE without FROM. The local fix preserves empty-output detection and now passes natively. The initial failure remains recorded.",
    "The initial not-null query logged PASS while fail-fast was cancelling it, but run_results marked it skipped; it was conservatively included in the follow-up.",
    "The follow-up wrapper initially rejected a naive local-preview timestamp versus an aware UTC result. Local reconciliation checked both against the earlier verified warehouse UTC timestamp and compared all captured columns without issuing another query. No source timestamp or expectation value was changed.",
    "An offline image rebuild lacked the dependency cache. The follow-up instead used the original pinned image and one read-only corrected SQL mount, checked offline before execution.",
    "This is execution evidence and focused self-review, not independent approval or independent practice."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Same-route equivalence remains an explicit assumption supported by source evidence; course IDs alone do not establish it.",
    "Absolute pace uses the common 21097 m convention; provider 21082 m metadata is retained in input provenance.",
    "Hourly ERA5 reanalysis at a venue proxy is matched to estimated runner midpoints, with one event start and no individual start offsets.",
    "Different runner fields and two editions do not isolate a causal weather effect.",
    "Real inputs ran through locally invoked Python/dbt against BigQuery, not Cloud Run or an orchestrator."
